## Task 5 backend: one-query series with server LTTB

Context: Runtime evidence on `bigcustomers` showed client pagination required
dozens of ordered scans and excessive transfer. The backend metric-series
contract now runs exactly one exhaustive ordered Databricks query per metric
and applies deterministic pure server-side LTTB sampling when the total exceeds
5,000 rows.

Changes:

1. tests/units/core/test_job_metrics.py
   Replaced paginated SQL expectations with one-query ordering contracts and
   added TDD coverage for threshold pass-through, exact 2,000-point sampling,
   first/last preservation, original one-based ranks, and deterministic output.
2. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_metric_series.py
   Replaced pagination payload contracts with compact exhaustive payload fields
   (`total`, `sampled`, `ranks`, `uris`, `labels`, `scores`) and added a guard
   test proving metric validation occurs before Databricks client construction.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py
   Removed pagination SQL helpers, added strict metric validation helper,
   switched to one exhaustive ordered query per metric, and implemented pure
   LTTB sampling with fixed `threshold=5000` and `sample_size=2000`.
4. src/back/core/graph_analysis/__init__.py
   Updated graph-analysis exports to remove obsolete pagination constants and
   expose the new metric validation and sampling helpers.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   Updated metric-series loading to validate metric before credentials/client
   setup, execute one exhaustive query, apply server-side LTTB, and serialize
   only the retained representative source rows with original ranks.
6. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Simplified `/dtwin/metrics/series` to metric-only input and aligned response
   shape with the new non-paginated backend contract.
7. .superpowers/sdd/task-5-backend-report.md
   Added implementation report with RED/GREEN evidence, final verification,
   commit metadata, concerns, and scope notes for backend-only delivery.

