Tests: Browser validation on `bigcustomers` loaded PageRank with one
`/dtwin/metrics/series?metric=pagerank` HTTP 200 request, no pagination
parameters, 222,207 transferred bytes, and 14.3 seconds from request start to
chart render. The response represented all 1,349,202 scored nodes with 2,000
retained LTTB points. This replaced the measured 54-request, approximately
137 MB, 5 minute 29 second baseline. Clustering abort completed in 0.23 seconds;
the cached PageRank chart restored in 1 ms with no request. Top N changed only
the table, logarithmic distributions remained enabled, Explorer click-through
worked, the 390 px viewport had no page overflow, and no Analytics JavaScript
errors were observed.
